    "content": "The CECAFA Kagame Cup 2026 concluded in Kigali, Rwanda, on August 8, with Somali referee Omar Abdulqadir Cartan taking charge of the tournament's final match. Cartan, an internationally accredited official, managed the game between Rayon Sports of Rwanda and Gor Mahia of Kenya, which ended in a 2-1 victory for the Rwandan side. This appointment marks a significant milestone for Somali football officiating on the regional stage.\n\nRayon Sports' win secured the coveted trophy for the host nation, capping off a competitive tournament that featured teams from across East and Central Africa. The final was closely contested, with both sides displaying strong attacking play, but Rayon Sports ultimately edged out their Kenyan opponents to claim the title.\n\nCartan's selection to referee the final reflects his standing within the regional football community and underscores the progress Somali referees have made in recent years. His ability to command a high-stakes match involving two top regional clubs is a testament to his skill and professionalism.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, this event carries particular relevance as it showcases a positive Somali contribution to the sport beyond national team participation. It offers a narrative of excellence and dedication that resonates with Somalis abroad, reinforcing the idea that Somali professionals can excel in international arenas.\n\nThe tournament also served as a platform for regional unity, bringing together nations with shared sporting interests. The smooth execution of the final, under Cartan's officiating, demonstrated the potential for further collaboration and exchange within the region's football infrastructure.\n\nRead the original report from Goobjoog here: https://goobjoog.com/2026/08/08/soomaaliya-oo-door-muuqda-ka-qaadatay-cecafa-kagame-cup-2026/",
