    "slug": "puntland-forces-take-control-of-federal-military-base-in-carmo",
    "summary": "Puntland administration announced it has taken over a military base in Carmo previously used by Somali federal forces, describing the move as part of security operations. The takeover occurred hours after federal troops vacated the facility.",
    "content": "In a significant development in Somalia's federal-state relations, the Puntland administration has announced that its police forces have assumed control of a military base in the town of Carmo, which had been used by Somali National Army troops. The handover was confirmed in a statement from Puntland Police, which characterized the operation as a security measure following the departure of federal soldiers from the base hours earlier.\n\nAccording to the statement, the operation was part of broader efforts to ensure stability in the area. Puntland authorities said they conducted thorough searches of the facility and the surrounding town to verify the security situation. The move comes amid ongoing tensions between the federal government of Somalia and regional administrations over the control of military assets and territory.\n\nA military source from the federal forces, who had been stationed at the base, indicated that the withdrawal was based on strategic considerations, though he declined to provide further details. The source said the troops had relocated from Carmo as part of a planned redeployment.\n\nThe takeover in Carmo is the latest in a series of incidents where Puntland has asserted its autonomy in security matters, often clashing with Mogadishu's authority. For the Somali diaspora, this event underscores the persistent challenges to federalism and unity in Somalia, which can affect stability and investment in the region. Diaspora communities often follow such developments closely as they may influence clan relations and the security of relatives back home.\n\nObservers note that the incident could further complicate efforts to integrate regional forces into a unified national security framework. While Puntland officials emphasized that the operation was peaceful, the move may be seen by some as a challenge to the federal government's sovereignty. The situation remains fluid, and it is unclear how the federal authorities will respond.\n\nRead the original report from Goobjoog here: https://goobjoog.com/2026/08/08/maamulka-puntland-oo-shaaciyay-inuu-la-wareegay-saldhiggii-ciidanka-federaalku-ay-ku lahaayeen-carmo/",
